  "notes": [
    {
      "topic": "admission",
      "text": "The Honors program is not modeled. Students must be a junior or senior in the major with an overall GPA of at least 3.00 and a philosophy GPA of 3.50, plan a program with a faculty advisor and the director of undergraduate studies before the first semester of senior year, complete three 300-level or higher courses including PHI 495 (honors thesis), and pass an oral examination."
    },
    {
      "topic": "advising",
      "text": "Undergraduate Research tracks are occasionally offered in Philosophy (seven courses over three years). Details are available from the Undergraduate Office. These tracks are not modeled."
    },
    {
      "topic": "advising",
      "text": "Students who would like to study abroad for a semester should consult the director of undergraduate studies. With the Department's permission, Philosophy majors may use credits from other study abroad programs to satisfy major requirements. This is not modeled as a substitution."
    },
    {
      "topic": "other",
      "text": "The major requires approximately 36 credits in total. Philosophy course descriptions are general and topics can vary between sections; see the department website for current details."
    },
    {
      "topic": "sbc",
      "text": "The SBC table lists optional major courses that can also satisfy SBC categories. These are per-course tags and are not modeled here."
    },
    {
      "topic": "other",
      "text": "The sample sequence lists PHI 395 and PHI 459 together in one 3-credit slot; only PHI 395 is transcribed as a course slot."
    }
  ],
